                                                                      ⟨f,g⟩=0

    The following result shows that µ1 and µ2 are continuous functions on the space K/ ∼ w.r.t. δ□ .

Theorem 3.3 (cf. [4, Theorem 6.6] or [25, Theorem 11.54]). Let {Ki }i∈N be a sequence of graphons
converging to K with respect to δ□ . Then as i → ∞,

                                µ1 (Ki ) → µ1 (K)           and      µ2 (Ki ) → µ2 (K).

