    We will prove Lemma 4.9 in a series of claims. We say that two distinct vertices in a graph
are true twins if they have the same closed neighbourhoods. We observe that G∗ cannot have true
twins.

Lemma 4.10. The graph G∗ is true-twin-free.

Proof. Suppose Ui , Uj ∈ V (G∗ ) are true twins. Then, by the eigenvalue-equation (4.1) for µ1 , we
have                                                 X
                             µ1 αi = ui αi + uj αj +    uℓ αℓ = µ1 αj ,
