    We observe that the subspace Λ2 (Rn ) is invariant under the linear transformation N .

Proposition 4.12. For all u, v ∈ Rn , we have

                                N (u ∧ v) = (M u) ∧ v + u ∧ (M v).

Proof. Recall that (A ⊗ B)(C ⊗ D) = AC ⊗ BD for any square matrices A, B, C, D of a given order.
Then

     N (u ∧ v) = (M ⊗ In + In ⊗ M ) (u ⊗ v − v ⊗ u)
               = (M ⊗ In )(u ⊗ v) + (In ⊗ M )(u ⊗ v) − (M ⊗ In )(v ⊗ u) − (In ⊗ M )(v ⊗ u)
               = (M u ⊗ v − v ⊗ M u) + (u ⊗ M v − M v ⊗ u)
               = (M u) ∧ v + u ∧ (M v).
